<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's foreign reserves slip to $8.054 bln.</title>
<headline>Colombia's foreign reserves slip to $8.054 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's net foreign reserves fell $4.1 million in the first week of September to a total of $8.054 billion, the central bank said.</p>
<p>It said the drop stemmed from the bank's short-term obligations abroad.</p>
<p>Colombia's net reserves have fallen by $270.4 million, or 3.2 percent, since December 30, 1995. On September 8 of last year, the country's net reserves stood at $8.215 billion.</p>
<p>-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
